content.text:
Now, the "roots" under platforms are good but some are giant dark rectangles/pillars. In cp2 they look like stalactites; acceptable. Let me make them wider at top and more tapered, with an irregular edge. Current points do. Fine.

The ledges: I think the biggest improvement now is adding a **top surface bevel** with a visible thickness and **cast shadow on the wall**. The top cap is 9px; at zoom 1.1 it's ~10px. Good. Add a **drop shadow** behind the platform onto the wall (down-right offset) to ground it. In drawLedge, currently contact shadow ellipse under; but for rotated platforms, the shadow should be drawn before the platform with an offset. Add at start:
```
ctx.save();
ctx.translate(10, 16);
poly(shape); fill rgba(0,0,0,.13); 
ctx.restore();
```
But drawn on top of the wall, offset down-right. This gives a shadow on the wall behind the ledge. Since the sun is on the left, shadow should go down-right. Great. Do it before the shape fill. That will help floating.

Add:
```
ctx.save();
ctx.translate(14, 18);
poly(shape);
ctx.fillStyle='rgba(4,10,12,.16)';
ctx.fill();
ctx.restore();
```
But this shadow will overlap the ledge itself? Drawn before the ledge, so hidden behind. Good.

Also, add a **soft ambient occlusion** under the platform (existing).

Let's implement.

